cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ffmpeg-dsf in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "ffmpeg-dsf"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The ffmpeg-dsf authors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dsd-toolbox/ffmpeg-dsf"
url: "https://github.com/dsd-toolbox/ffmpeg-dsf"
abstract: "Patches for FFmpeg that fix the channel layout of DSF channel type 5, add a DSF muxer, and add the libdsdupsample encoder (PCM to DSD64, DSD128 or DSD256 through the dsd-upsample C library). The encoder's DSF output is byte-identical to the dsd-upsample command-line tool of the same library release, except for two documented header fields."
# The patches (patches/) are LGPL-2.1-or-later, FFmpeg's licence; the other files are
# MIT OR Apache-2.0, the documentation CC BY 4.0 (README.md, "Licence and credits"). Zenodo
# reads `license` as a single SPDX string, so only the patches' licence is given here.
license: LGPL-2.1-or-later
version: "0.1.0"
keywords:
  - "DSD"
  - "DSF"
  - "FFmpeg"
  - "audio"
  - "muxer"
  - "encoder"
